18.36.054.343 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"status\": \"answered\",\n  \"answer\": \"A balanced chemical equation provides several important pieces of information. First, it shows the reactants and products involved in the reaction through their chemical symbols and formulae. Second, it indicates the ratio of molecules of reactants and products, which helps in understanding the stoichiometry of the reaction. Third, it gives the relative masses of the reactants and products, which is useful for calculating the amounts of substances involved. Additionally, it can show the physical states of the substances, whether the reaction is exothermic or endothermic, and any gas evolved or precipitate formed. These details make the chemical equation more informative and help in predicting the outcomes of chemical reactions.\",\n  \"selected_evidence_ids\": [\"E1\", \"E3\", \"E4\", \"E5\"],\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E1\",\n      \"pdf_page\": 35,\n      \"textbook_page\": 25\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E3\",\n      \"pdf_page\": 38,\n      \"textbook_page\": 28\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E4\",\n      \"pdf_page\": 40,\n      \"textbook_page\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E5\",\n      \"pdf_page\": 43,\n      \"textbook_page\": 33\n    }\n  ],\n  \"missing_information\": []\n}"}
