20.17.988.327 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"status\": \"answered\",\n  \"answer\": \"Tooth decay starts when the pH of the mouth is lower than 5.5 because the acidic environment corrodes tooth enamel. Tooth enamel, made of calcium phosphate, is the hardest substance in the body. However, it can be corroded when the pH in the mouth is below 5.5. This happens because bacteria in the mouth produce acids by breaking down sugar and food particles. These acids lower the pH, making the environment more acidic. The lower pH means there are more hydrogen ions (H3O+), which can dissolve the calcium phosphate in the enamel, leading to tooth decay. To prevent this, it is important to maintain a neutral or slightly basic pH in the mouth, which can be achieved by cleaning the mouth after eating and using toothpaste that neutralizes acids.\",\n  \"selected_evidence_ids\": [\"E2\"],\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E2\",\n      \"pdf_page\": 59,\n      \"textbook_page\": 49\n    }\n  ],\n  \"missing_information\": []\n}"}
